/*
------------------------------------------------------------
Problem    : Swap Nodes in Pairs
Platform   : LeetCode
Topic      : Linked List
Difficulty : Medium

Problem:
Given the head of a linked list, swap every two adjacent
nodes and return the head of the modified list.

The values inside the nodes cannot be modified. Only the
node connections may be changed.

Approach:
Use recursion to swap one pair of nodes at a time.

The first two nodes are swapped, and the remaining linked
list is recursively processed. The head of the swapped
remaining list is then connected to the current pair.

The second node becomes the new head of the current pair,
while the first node becomes the second node after swapping.

Why does this work?

Every recursive call is responsible for swapping exactly one
pair of adjacent nodes.

Once the current pair is swapped, recursion correctly handles
the remaining linked list and returns its new head. Connecting
the swapped pair with the recursively processed list produces
the final correctly swapped linked list.

Algorithm:
1. Handle the base case where fewer than two nodes remain.
2. Store references to the first and second nodes.
3. Recursively swap the remaining linked list.
4. Connect the first node to the swapped remaining list.
5. Make the second node point to the first node.
6. Return the second node as the new head.

Time Complexity : O(n)

Reason:
Each node is visited exactly once.

Space Complexity : O(n)

Reason:
The recursive calls use stack space proportional to the
number of nodes.

------------------------------------------------------------
*/

class Solution {
public:
    ListNode* swapPairs(ListNode* head) {

        // If fewer than two nodes remain,
        // no swapping is required.
        if (head == nullptr || head->next == nullptr) {
            return head;
        }

        // The first two nodes to be swapped.
        ListNode* firstNode = head;
        ListNode* secondNode = head->next;

        // Recursively swap the remaining linked list.
        firstNode->next = swapPairs(secondNode->next);

        // Complete the swap.
        secondNode->next = firstNode;

        // The second node becomes the new head.
        return secondNode;
    }
};
